WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.589
Aerial perspective can reveal people, homes, routines, property, sensitive locations, and security features that were not the mission's purpose.

00:00:09.589 --> 00:00:18.710
Public visibility from above does not remove privacy expectations or the risk created by recording, aggregation, and distribution.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.750
Apply data minimization before launch.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:31.339
Bound the area, aim sensors carefully, choose no more detail than needed, and avoid unnecessary people or private spaces.

00:00:31.339 --> 00:00:39.056
If sensitive content is captured incidentally, restrict access and follow approved review and deletion procedures.

00:00:39.056 --> 00:00:42.564
Use requires legitimate authority and proportionality.

00:00:42.564 --> 00:00:54.024
Do not use aerial observation for stalking, harassment, targeting private individuals, unlawful surveillance, flight-restriction bypass, interference with aircraft, or evasion of accountable oversight.

00:00:54.024 --> 00:00:58.935
Reporting can create harm even when collection was lawful.

00:00:58.935 --> 00:01:07.121
Avoid publishing precise sensitive locations, identifiable people, access vulnerabilities, or raw imagery without a defined need.

00:01:07.121 --> 00:01:11.564
Use redaction, aggregation, or controlled distribution when appropriate.

00:01:11.564 --> 00:01:18.814
Access control should separate pilots, analysts, clients, administrators, and public recipients according to need.

00:01:18.814 --> 00:01:22.790
Protect accounts, storage, exports, and sharing links.

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:27.701
Record who approved collection and who received sensitive products.

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:30.274
Responsible use is explainable.

00:01:30.274 --> 00:01:38.459
The operator should be able to state the purpose, authority, boundaries, evidence, uncertainty, retention, and safeguards.

00:01:38.459 --> 00:01:45.242
When safety, legality, privacy, or ethics are unclear, stop and seek qualified guidance.
